course: dictionary
lesson: 14926
title: The word refurbishment
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A refurbishment is work that makes a place or a thing look and work like new again. The word comes from «refurbish», which means to do up or fix up. Look for the clues around it: «The library is closed for refurbishment» tells you the library is closed while workers make it better.
explain: The clues often sit in the words nearby. «The school hall is getting a major refurbishment this summer» tells you the job is big, because the word major means large or important. A refurbishment usually means repairing, cleaning and painting, not building something brand new.
explain: The word can also be about a used machine. «Sam's old laptop was sold after a refurbishment, so it works like new and costs less.» Here a refurbishment means someone fixed up a used machine so it can be sold again. Check your meaning by putting it in the sentence: the laptop was fixed up, so the sentence still makes sense.
fact: A refurbishment is the work of repairing, cleaning and redecorating a building or room.
fact: «Closed for refurbishment» is a sign you will often see on shops, libraries and swimming pools.
fact: «Refurbished» means a used phone, laptop or machine that has been fixed up and can be sold again.
fact: «Undergo a refurbishment» means to have a refurbishment done.
fact: Use the clues: if a place is closed for refurbishment, workers are probably making it look and work like new.
exercise: «The library is closed for refurbishment.» What does refurbishment mean here? | A kind of hot drink | A party for the new year | *The work of repairing, cleaning and redecorating so it looks new | A quiet, sad place to rest
exercise: «The school hall is getting a major refurbishment this summer.» Which word tells you the job is big? | summer | getting | school | *major
exercise: Sam bought a refurbished laptop. What does refurbished suggest? | A laptop with no screen | A brand new laptop that has never been switched on | A laptop made of wood | *A used laptop that was fixed up and sold again
test: «The café is closed for refurbishment this week.» Why is the café closed? | It has run out of cake | It is closed every day of the year | *It is being repaired and redecorated | It is holding a birthday party
test: Which of these is a refurbishment? | Reading a book about pools | Swimming in the pool on a sunny day | Buying a new towel for the pool | *Painting and fixing up an old pool so it looks new
exam: Which best explains refurbishment? | Eating a large meal at the café | *Making a used place or thing look and work like new | Running very fast to win a race | Losing something in a shop
